<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Birkebeiner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1174">1174</a>–<a href="/years/1217">1217</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Birchlegs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Birkebeiner (&quot;birch-legs&quot;, from the birch bark some wore as footwear) were a rebel party in the Norwegian civil wars, formed in 1174 among poor and landless men. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sverre-of-norway">Sverre Sigurdsson</a> from 1177 they defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-erlingsson">Magnus Erlingsson</a> and became the royal party. Their descendants put Haakon IV on the throne, and their heritage is commemorated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>'s Birkebeiner ski race.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/birkebeiner.jpg" alt="Birkebeiner" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Knud Bergslien · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Birkebeinerne_p%C3%A5_Ski_over_Fjeldet_med_Kongsbarnet_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
